1.0.1 2026-10-14
  - Added stimuli/stimuli.tsv and stimuli.json: one row per stim_id with properties and SHA-256 of the BMD stimulus_set MP4 file of the same number (no media added).
  - README: section 'Stimuli' (how to obtain the BMD videos, join, missing audio track in the BMD MP4 files); the presented audio most likely came from another version of each clip, labelled as an inference).
  - task-video_events.json: stim_id joins stimuli/stimuli.tsv.
  - .bidsignore: REUSE_METADATA.md (not a BIDS file; validator NOT_INCLUDED error).
  - dataset_description.json: GeneratedBy entry for this enrichment.
  - dataset_description.json: HowToAcknowledge and the 'Paper' entry of ReferencesAndLinks, which held '?' placeholders, now give the EMD paper (Gifford et al. 2026, arXiv doi:10.48550/arXiv.2608.28768), as in upstream OpenNeuro ds008257 1.0.1.
  - README: the EMD citation (title and DOI placeholders filled), the subject-3 eye-tracking calibration note of upstream 1.0.1, a pointer to REUSE_METADATA.md.
  - Added REUSE_METADATA.md: source and archive identity (recordings unchanged from OpenNeuro 1.0.0; upstream 1.0.1 changes only CHANGES, README and dataset_description.json), event-stimulus join, annotation provenance, caveats, stimulus access, channel status.
  - Added one *_channels.tsv per EEG run (768 files; the source has none): name, type, units, status, status_description in BrainVision header order; 88 channel-runs in 74 runs marked bad under rule emd-bads-v1 (see REUSE_METADATA.md).
  - task-video_eeg.json: EEGChannelCount 128 -> 127. The headers list 127 recorded channels; the 128th electrode, Fz,
    is the online reference (EEGReference Fz, unchanged).
  - Added code/check_channels.py: checks every channels.tsv against its BrainVision header and recomputes rule
    emd-bads-v1 from the signal.
  - dataset_description.json: Version 1.0.0 -> 1.0.1.

